-- title:
--   Fricke involutions intertwining the degeneracy maps at level Mℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, let $\ell$ be a prime, let $\iota\colon\overline{\mathbb Q}\to\mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism, and let $W,W'\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$ have matrices $\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\ M&0\end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\ M\ell&0\end{pmatrix}$. Write $F=$ [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionFieldBar M H`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L123) for the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(M)$ (the subgroup of matrices in $\Gamma_0(M)$ whose lower-right entry reduces into $H$), and $F'$ for the corresponding base change of [`ModularCurve.xHTopFunctionFieldC ℚ M H (M * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L84), the field generated by ratios of integral forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell)$. The assertion is that there exist $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphisms $w$ of $F$ and $w'$ of $F'$ with the following properties. First, for every $x\in F$, every $k\in\mathbb Z$ and all weight-$k$ modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$, if $\iota(x)$ (coefficientwise application of $\iota$) times the width-one $q$-expansion of $g$ equals that of $f$, then $\iota(w\,x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k W$ equals that of $f\mid_k W$; likewise for $w'$, $F'$, forms on $\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell)$ and $W'$. Secondly, $w'\circ\alpha=\beta\circ w$ and $w'\circ\beta=\alpha\circ w$ on $F$, where $\alpha=$ [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaHBar`](def/ModularCurve_XHHeckeOperator.html#L66) is the inclusion $F\subseteq F'$ and $\beta=$ [`ModularCurve.heckeBetaHBar`](def/ModularCurve_XHHeckeOperator.html#L118) is the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ when that map sends the function field of $\Gamma_H(M)$ into that of $\Gamma_H(M)\cap\Gamma_0(M\ell)$, and the inclusion otherwise. Finally, $w\circ w=\mathrm{id}_F$ and $w'\circ w'=\mathrm{id}_{F'}$.
--
--   This is the Fricke (Atkin–Lehner) involution $w_M$ on $X_H(M)$ together with its partner $w_{M\ell}$ at the larger level, described on function fields of Laurent series and characterised by pull-back along $\tau\mapsto-1/(M\tau)$ on ratios of modular forms; the two degeneracy embeddings $\alpha$ (inclusion) and $\beta$ ($q\mapsto q^{\ell}$) are interchanged by conjugation with these involutions. It feeds the corresponding statement over the residue field used in the analysis of Hecke correspondences at level $M\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_algEquiv_pair_xHFunctionFieldBar_slash_fricke_intertwines_heckeAlphaHBar_heckeBetaHBar.lean

